  "worked_solution": "The number is *negative* because it is to the *left* of zero.\n\nThe absolute value of the number is $5.6,$ so the distance between that number and zero on a number line is $5.6.$ \n\nThe negative number at a distance of $5.6$ from zero is $-5.6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14145654/assets/c0341fe4a55e5b0bb6b6f464f3b8d21c8c867a9e80d6dfb2fe7feea8c60c7dd5.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
